WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.490
Hey, Raquel.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:42.280
Hey, if we hang around here, Natalie's 
gonna do something to us again.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.450
I suppose...

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.660
I don't know what's got you so interested.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.330
Can you tell what this 
stuff is just by looking?

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.540
No, not at all.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.500
But they said that people 
in the past fought the gods

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.260
by using this machinery

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.340
to facilitate the abilities of 
people with precognitive powers.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.680
Yeah, they said something 
about them being betrayed...

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.220
From what Miss Eirote tells me,

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.560
all of this works by conveying 
complicated instructions

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.390
that are built up from sets 
of simple calculations.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.210
That's exactly the same way 
that magic works, isn't it?

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.530
I wouldn't know...

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:18.450
Hey, you two. We'll be reaching 
the coast of Sauer soon.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.500
Come up to the command deck.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.250
C'mon, Raquel, let's go back.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.010
If we're late, old Tomboy 
Senes is gonna throw a fit.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.050
She'll go, "Grrr!"

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.640
Yes, of course...

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.220
I can hear you, you little brat!

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.310
What's wrong? Feeling nostalgic 
about the old homeland?

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.390
Not really.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.230
The village you three grew up 
in must've been a nice place.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.440
You know our village?

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.690
No. I just get that feeling 
when I look at you three.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:03:00.070
It must be nice to have a 
place you want to go back to.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:12.460
"Opera of Powers and Plots"

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.290
We find ourselves in a difficult situation.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.380
The Giat Empire's special weapon, the Skid,

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.920
has breached our territorial waters.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.550
This is a clear act of invasion.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.140
We, the Leinwan Royal Forces, must 
meet this threat with resolve

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.850
and smash it utterly.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.680
But... they say that the Skid

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.850
is a fortress built by the demons 
in the age of the Genesis Wars.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:36.610
Wouldn't any attempt to take it by force 
involve a fair number of difficulties?

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:40.190
True, we will most likely be unable to 
destroy it with a standard cannon attack.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.530
Which is why I propose the use

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.410
of the strategic grade 
offensive spell Ginnungagap.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.450
But Ginnungagap is...

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.830
As I recall, that spell is banned by treaty.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.280
We should uphold the treaty 
and let our country fall?

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.960
This is an invasion.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.840
Gentlemen, we should 
destroy the Skid utterly,

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.470
and then proceed to march on Giat.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.590
One moment, please, General Peters-Stahl.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.180
You have something to add, Lady Bairach?

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.930
I have heard that the Skid set out on its own

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.140
after trading fire with its 
own country's Second Fleet.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:15.600
It is possible that the Skid's crew 
was seen as a rebel force by Giat,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.070
and they sent out the fleet to pursue.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.860
Perhaps it is premature to conclude 
that this is an invasion.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.280
What if that was merely camouflage 
meant to distract us?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.620
If their main forces arrive and 
begin a joint assault with the Skid,

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.200
it will be too late for us to act.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.290
Which is exactly why I believe that 
ascertaining the truth is crucial.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.690
If we break the treaty,

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.790
a plunge into all-out war is inevitable.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.740
We will use up our military 
forces for nothing.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.760
You believe our forces will be 
defeated by the likes of Giat?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.310
Fortune sometimes decides the battle.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.890
Well, well, well.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.060
Those are hardly the words I would 
expect to hear from the woman

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.600
who controls the most powerful Special 
Forces unit in the Royal Forces.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.600
Justice is on our side.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:01.320
That Skid is harboring the poison that will 
destroy the world. The Scrapped Princess.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.720
For the sake of public order and 
peace, not only in our own country,

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.780
but the entire world, we must eliminate her.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.120
This is a holy war.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.200
Isn't that right, Cardinal Hogue?

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.250
Indeed.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.370
Do whatever you must.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.510
There isn't a moment to lose! Kill her!

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:18.920
Kill the Scrapped Princess!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.050
What do you intend to do?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.170
I will get ready and stand 
by to receive orders.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.010
I see. I suppose that's all we can do.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.930
We are soldiers, after all.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:34.600
What are you afraid of?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.100
Lady Steyr!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.750
Everything is going according to plan.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.860
The Scrapped Princess will die soon.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:45.460
But just to be safe, keep agitating 
the King just as you've been doing.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.280
Understand?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.810
Yes, my lady!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.530
A strategic grade offensive spell...

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.200
It turned out just like 
Jill predicted, didn't it?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:59.210
Our country will be in a state 
of war with Giat before long.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:02.280
You will probably receive 
operation orders, too.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.300
Chris?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.260
I should report this to Prince Forsyth.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.730
Everyone seems oddly on edge, don't they?

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:20.650
Yes...

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:22.820
Well, there are a lot of 
people in the capital,

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.860
so maybe it's always like this.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:28.320
For now, let's hurry and go to 
your friend's house, shall we?

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.200
R-Right!

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.910
Father! Please reconsider what you're doing!

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:36.580
We mustn't throw away the lives of our 
precious soldiers in a needless war!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.160
Silence!

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.560
Don't look at us with those eyes.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.130
You have your mother's eyes.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.340
She disobeyed our command and 
allowed our daughter to escape!

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.050
Your sister almost certainly 
has the same eyes, as well.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.100
He wouldn't listen to me, just as I expected.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:56.970
Oh, I see...

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.310
Father is going to throw 
countless subjects into a war

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:04.440
just so he can kill the Scrapped 
Princess. So he can kill my sister...

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.820
What in the world is Father thinking?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.810
What's the matter, Miss Winia?

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.130
It's nothing.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.990
I was just thinking to myself 
that this is a huge house.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.160
You think so?

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.300
For a baronial family estate,

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.330
I think the design is rather 
pedestrian, personally.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.130
Still, it's odd for there to 
be no guards manning the gate.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:29.060
Um... Do you know a lot 
about noble estates, Leo?

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:31.090
Oh, I never told you?

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:35.970
I'm the eldest son of Baron Skorpus, 
lord of the barony of Takos.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.100
I'm on a training tour at the moment, though.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.930
Oh, I didn't know.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.100
This puts us in a bind...

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.060
We can't simply barge in unannounced.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:46.520
I suppose I'll just have to 
stand here and shout until...

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.020
Um... That's all right.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:54.280
It would be rude to come 
see him without warning.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:54.990
I'd be a bother.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.990
Don't talk like that!

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.250
Wanting to see someone is a precious feeling!

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:03.060
How could you give up over 
a little setback like this?!

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:07.000
Or so I'm sure Miss Pacifica 
would say if she were here...

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:17.300
Chris...

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.230
Um, I...

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.820
Baron Bairach!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.460
Miss Winia...

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.630
It's okay.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:59.100
I'm sure he has a good reason.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.600
Or is that putting too positive a spin on it?

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.120
No, that's just fine. That's the right idea.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.060
Okay.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:13.740
What? Ginnungagap?!

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.570
That's crazy! Are they serious?

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.360
The ship may be offshore,

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.740
but the people who live on the coast 
aren't going to walk away unscathed!

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.250
This is the official order 
from His Majesty the King.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.580
Please begin your stage 
1 incantations at once.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.180
There's no sign of activity at all.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.430
What do they think they're doing, calling 
us here and then making us wait?

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.560
Pacifica? Are you all right?

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:50.440
Yeah... I'm a little scared, that's all.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.900
The Peacemakers can't attack 
Pacifica directly, right?

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:57.860
Right. They will probably 
use humans to attack her.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.370
Maybe they don't know we're here.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.780
We should signal them or...

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:02.950
What are you, an idiot?!

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:06.580
They can detect our movements 
whenever they want!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:07.910
Yeah, I guess I am!

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:11.790
Well, as long as the Skid's 
defensive functions are online,

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:14.250
they could fire a million 
large-bore cannonballs at us,

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.960
and it still wouldn't dent us.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.380
Do not let your guard down.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.970
The Peacemakers are fully aware of 
the capabilities of this fortress.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:24.350
It is safe to assume that they are avoiding 
unnecessary combat for that reason.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.470
You've got guts, showing your face to me.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:31.560
Or don't demons have that 
kind of sensitivity...

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.020
That <i>hurt</i>, you little twerp!

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.070
How can you talk to her like that?!

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:38.920
If it weren't for Zefiris, 
you'd still be brainwashed!

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:41.570
I wouldn't have been brainwashed 
in the <i>first </i>place

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.620
if she hadn't been working 
in cahoots with Natalie!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:44.580
And it's not just that.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.910
Even knowing everything, 
she was trying to use us.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.240
That might be true,

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.500
but Zefiris has problems of her own!

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.960
Well, there's no point in 
fighting with you here.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.270
What are the Peacemakers after?

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.430
Probably a strategic grade offensive spell.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.780
Strategic grade? What's that?

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.660
It must be Ginnungagap.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.580
Is that what Reynard was trying 
to cast in the heretic village?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.870
The principles are the same.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.890
But if highly trained wizards cast it,

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:35.630
its power should be immeasurably greater.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.720
Hey, wait a minute.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.730
Those things are supposed 
to be banned by treaty.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:43.980
Treaties mean nothing in the 
face of Peacemaker mind control.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:46.680
That treaty was promulgated by the 
Peacemakers in the first place

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.430
via the Church of Mauser.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.270
Still, incantations for strategic 
grade spells take a long time,

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.400
and you can't fire them 
off in quick succession.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:58.980
I think the Skid's defensive functions 
should be able to withstand it.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:11:59.780
They can.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:03.490
But the Peacemakers are 
aware of that fact, as well.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:11.710
This is taking forever...

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:12.760
We have time to kill,

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:16.380
so why don't we release a few 
proxies inside the capital?

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:19.870
Don't. Tactics like that are pointless.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:21.170
Cz...

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:25.340
I think you may have spent a little too 
much time stuck halfway uncompressed.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:26.930
What do you mean by that?

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.530
You want to avoid human 
deaths if at all possible.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:31.100
Isn't that what you're thinking?

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.140
We're Peacemakers.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:37.530
We're programmed to preserve the 
human race in a stable state,

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:38.440
so it's only natural.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:39.880
Is it?

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.320
Your thinking seems awfully human to me.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.570
Right, Socom?

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.060
Perhaps so.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:48.410
But Cz's opinion does have merit.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:52.290
They have already begun 
the spell's incantation.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.920
There is no need for us to 
resort to cheap tricks here.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:59.890
Sheesh, you Artillery-types are 
about as subtle as a hammer.

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:01.400
Brute force is all well and good,

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.010
but doesn't guile give you more of a thrill?

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.930
<i>You're </i>the one who thinks 
too much like a human.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:10.720
I would prefer to avoid overt intervention 
on our part as much as possible.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:14.020
As we planned, suppressing 
the mobile fortress'

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:17.310
defense and mobility functions 
should be sufficient.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:21.400
Here we are, three Peacemakers, and 
we're resorting to parlor tricks.

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:24.490
I want to carry out the task in the most 
efficient manner possible, that's all.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:27.360
I'm not interested in taking 
pleasure in needless flashiness.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.700
Fine, fine...

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:35.410
Princess Senes, defense 
system output is dropping.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:36.500
I can't maintain shields!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.350
What? What's causing it?

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.000
Unknown.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.370
There doesn't appear to be any damage 
from an outside source, though.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.400
You don't think it's Natalie, do you?

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.470
It isn't me.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.820
You expect us to believe you?

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.390
With Pacifica Cassul aboard this ship,

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.810
I have no reason to expose 
her to danger, do I?

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.580
Well, that's true...

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:57.940
The impression I get is 
that the system is being

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.520
ripped apart at the seams 
by some invisible force.

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:03.280
Invisible force? Is it the Peacemakers?

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.900
Yes, of course. It's being 
controlled remotely.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.860
You must get away from here, Senes Lur Giat.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:09.820
I should <i>what</i>?

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.700
If we take a direct hit from 
a strategic grade spell

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.040
with our defense functions locked down,

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.450
we won't walk away unscathed.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:19.120
Get serious! Those Peacemakers 
are here, right?

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.960
You want me to run when the people who 
killed my men are right under my nose?!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:25.170
You would be killed by the humans 
that the Peacemakers control

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.270
long before you had a chance to fight them.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.720
Damn it... Withdraw, full speed!

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:34.390
Roger!

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:39.640
What's wrong? What're you doing?!

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.060
It's not working! We're not moving!

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.360
What? How could we not be moving?

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.730
<i>Do </i>something!

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.530
Big sister...

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:47.740
I recommend that you abandon ship.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:51.820
You little... You expect us to sit back 
and watch the people in the capital die?

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.870
I believe that I understand how you feel.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:59.030
But this fortress is now nothing more than 
a large target floating in the water.

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:01.800
If you stay here, Pacifica will die.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.420
And the rest of you with her.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.420
I expect that such an outcome 
would also be undesirable to you.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:16.950
I'll fight the Peacemakers with the Dragoon.

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:19.410
If their grip on the ship loosens,

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.140
we should be able to move again, right?

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:25.010
Yes, but there are three Peacemakers here.

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:27.110
In terms of combat power, we 
are completely outmatched.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:28.740
So what?!

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.320
Cz is with them.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.660
If you are going to fight, you 
will have no chance of winning

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.870
unless you are prepared to 
utterly destroy your enemy.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.250
Can you fight Cz and not hold back?

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:40.330
Yeah.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.700
Shannon Cassul...

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.130
Don't do anything stupid.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:48.710
Sure.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.740
Let's go.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:01.890
Give me all the power you have 
access to right now, Zefiris.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:03.440
That is dangerous.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:06.110
You still have misgivings towards me.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:09.030
Doing that in a state of incomplete fusion 
would put a strain on your body that...

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:10.990
Is this any time to be holding back?!

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.230
As you wish.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.020
What's that?

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.310
That is a Dragoon in its true form.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.740
Here they come.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:54.360
So, she's finally taken 
physical form. Interesting.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:58.370
The two of you can maintain control 
of the mobile fortress by yourselves?

00:16:58.370 --> 00:16:59.580
We can keep it from moving, anyway.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.160
In that case, I'll handle the Dragoon.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.420
Manifest class two divine retribution 
enforcement configuration.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.600
It's Cz.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:25.440
Cin...

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:36.070
Defense systems back up to 20%.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.780
Divert all power to engines 
and try to break away.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.280
This is our chance. Cz will 
be focused on the battle.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:43.160
All right, maximum output!

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.120
Roger!

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:52.340
They're putting up a fight...

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:52.960
It's no use.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.030
Stop it, Cin! I don't want to...

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:09.350
Silence! If you want to say 
something to an opponent,

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:13.480
do it after you've crushed them 
underfoot with overwhelming force!

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:29.710
Barrier, protect us!

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.720
Big sister...

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:39.860
Pacifica!

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.270
Oh, no!

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.210
That completes our mission 
for the time being...

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:11.370
Destructive effect of the strategic 
grade offensive spell Ginnungagap

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:14.110
has taken effect above the Giat 
Army's special weapon, the Skid.

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:16.420
Half of the ship has been destroyed.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:19.050
A search for survivors is 
being carried out by magic,

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.410
but no life signs have been 
detected at this point.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:24.010
We believe the threat from the target 
has been completely eliminated.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:25.460
Good work.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.360
They used Ginnungagap without 
giving any warning, huh?

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:40.610
They'll do anything in 
the name of the mission,

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:43.360
even if the explosion triggers a tsunami.

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:46.410
I see the military's M.O. hasn't changed.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:08.030
Um... Who are you?

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:12.480
When you ask that question, aren't you 
supposed to give your own name first?

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:14.530
Yeah, that's probably right, but...

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:16.360
Well, I can't remember anything.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.820
My name, or anything else.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.280
Hey, do you know who I am?

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:22.010
Sorry, I don't know you.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:23.330
Oh. Darn.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:25.490
See you.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.160
Hey, why are you following me?

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:40.640
Because I don't know anyone else,

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:44.130
and if I go with you, I might 
run into someone who knows me.

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:45.610
Suit yourself.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.850
So, what's your name?

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:49.910
Furet.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.560
For someone who can't remember anything, 
you sure seem to be in a good mood.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:58.440
You think so?

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.630
In that case, maybe I'm 
better off not remembering!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:37.080
The Skid has been destroyed, and the 
three Cassul siblings have been split up.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:39.620
Shannon and Raquel frantically 
search for Pacifica,

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:42.340
but Pacifica has no idea of the 
trouble they're going through,

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:44.800
and has been living a carefree 
life with a boy named Furet.

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:47.380
It's important for humans to kick back 
and relax once in a while, isn't it?

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:48.650
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:49.720
"Duet by the Riverside."

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
